        <div class="insights-grid">
          <div class="insight-card">
            <div class="insight-icon" style="background: rgba(249,115,22,0.12);">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f97316" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2C6.5 2 2 6.5 2 12s4.5 10 10 10 10-4.5 10-10S17.5 2 12 2"/><path d="M12 8v4l3 3"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="insight-title">Waste Heat Dominance</div>
            <div class="insight-body">167.7 EJ is lost as waste or rejected heat — more than twice all renewable inputs combined (73.7 EJ). This single flow represents the largest output stream in the global energy system.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="insight-card">
            <div class="insight-icon" style="background: rgba(107,114,128,0.12);">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="7"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7"/><rect x="3" y="14" width="7" height="7"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="insight-title">Fossil Fuel Dominance</div>
            <div class="insight-body">Oil (170.5 EJ), Coal (157.3 EJ), and Natural Gas (141.5 EJ) together supply ~469 EJ — over 78% of total primary energy input, flowing primarily through thermal power and refining.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="insight-card">
            <div class="insight-icon" style="background: rgba(16,185,129,0.12);">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 100 20A10 10 0 0012 2z"/><path d="M8 12s1.5-2 4-2 4 2 4 2"/><path d="M9 9h.01"/><path d="M15 9h.01"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="insight-title">Thin Renewable Streams</div>
            <div class="insight-body">Hydro (15.8 EJ), Wind (8.4 EJ), Solar (5.9 EJ), Biomass (42.6 EJ), and Geothermal (1.0 EJ) combined represent only ~12% of total primary energy. Their narrow flows contrast starkly with fossil fuel bands.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="insight-card">
            <div class="insight-icon" style="background: rgba(59,130,246,0.12);">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"><path d="M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="insight-title">Transport &amp; Industry Lead</div>
            <div class="insight-body">Transport (122.7 EJ) and Industry (154.6 EJ) absorb the largest end-use shares. Transport is driven almost entirely by oil refining, while Industry draws from direct use, electricity, and petroleum products.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="source-note">
        Data: Approximate 2022 global energy balance based on IEA World Energy Outlook and LLNL energy flow estimates. Minor balancing discrepancies may exist due to rounding. Values in exajoules (EJ). 1 EJ = 10¹⁸ joules ≈ 277.8 TWh.
      </p>

